WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
So far, we have covered how to recognize cardiac arrest

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.760
and how to perform high-quality CPR on your own.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.320
Now, we are going to add a powerful tool to our rescue,

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.400
the AED, or automated external defibrillator.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.400
An AED is a portable device

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.959
that can actually analyze a heart's rhythm

00:00:18.959 --> 00:00:21.520
and, if necessary, deliver a shock

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.180
to help restore a normal heartbeat.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.920
It doesn't just shock, however.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.860
The AED will also guide you

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.340
through chest compressions and breaths

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.779
while turning on a metronome to help you maintain rhythm.

00:00:33.779 --> 00:00:35.400
Think of it as a smart assistant

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.660
that talks you through every single step

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.099
with clear and simple voice prompts.

00:00:40.099 --> 00:00:41.520
They are designed to be simple

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.119
for non-medical bystanders to use.

00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:45.740
When you open an AED,

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.660
you will usually find a small kit inside

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.419
to help you prepare the patient.

00:00:49.419 --> 00:00:52.060
This typically includes gloves for your safety,

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.139
scissors to cut through clothing and expose the bare chest,

00:00:55.259 --> 00:00:58.419
and a small towel to wipe away any sweat or water.

00:00:58.419 --> 00:01:00.220
You might even find a razor.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.259
If a person has a very hairy chest,

00:01:02.259 --> 00:01:04.239
the pads might not stick properly,

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:06.339
so you can use the razor to quickly shave

00:01:06.339 --> 00:01:08.980
just the spots where the pads need to go.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.360
Using the AED is as simple as following these steps.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.940
First, turn it on and apply the pads to the bare chest

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.900
as soon as it is available.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.300
As soon as it is turned on,

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.779
the AED will begin giving you audible instructions.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.820
Second, check your pad placement

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.779
against the pictures provided on the pads themselves.

00:01:27.779 --> 00:01:30.540
Third, listen carefully to the voice prompts.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.900
If the device says shock advised,

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.099
make sure no one is touching the person.

00:01:35.099 --> 00:01:38.360
Shout clear, loudly, and look to ensure everyone is back

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.220
before you press the shock button.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.540
The AED will never shock on its own.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.660
Your instructor is going to demonstrate

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.940
how to use the Trainer AED now,

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.320
and then you'll have a chance to try it yourself

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.779
and ask any questions.

